###
### ========================================
### NOTES FOR TESTING
### ========================================

# 1. Before running requests:
#    - Ensure API is running on https://localhost:7001
#    - Install "REST Client" extension in VS Code
#    - Create .env file with actual JWT token from login response

# 2. JWT Token Flow:
#    - Register a new user → Get userId
#    - Login with credentials → Get JWT token and refresh token
#    - Copy JWT token to @token variable
#    - Use in all protected endpoints

# 3. Test Database Roles:
#    - 1 = Admin
#    - 2 = User
#    - 3 = Moderator
#    - 4 = Guest

# 4. External Provider IDs:
#    - 1 = Google
#    - 2 = Facebook
#    - 3 = GitHub

# 5. Password Requirements:
#    - Minimum 8 characters
#    - At least one uppercase letter (A-Z)
#    - At least one lowercase letter (a-z)
#    - At least one digit (0-9)
#    - At least one special character (!@#$%^&*)

# 6. Expected HTTP Status Codes:
#    - 200 OK: Successful operation
#    - 201 Created: Resource created successfully
#    - 400 Bad Request: Validation errors
#    - 401 Unauthorized: Missing or invalid token
#    - 403 Forbidden: Insufficient permissions
#    - 404 Not Found: Resource not found
#    - 500 Internal Server Error: Server error

# 7. Logging:
#    All requests are logged in application logs
#    Location: C:\Program Files\Manam\logs\manam-api-YYYY-MM-DD.txt

# 8. Soft Delete:
#    When you delete a user, the account is marked as deleted
#    but not permanently removed from the database
#    IsDeleted = 1, DeletedAt = current timestamp
#    Can be restored if needed

# 9. Rate Limiting (Future):
#    Login endpoint will have rate limiting
#    Max 5 attempts per minute per IP address
#    Account lockout after 5 failed attempts

# 10. Two-Factor Authentication (Future):
#     Will require TOTP or SMS verification after login
#     Additional endpoint: /authentication/verify-2fa
